                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "319085eb-cc17-31d6-83d0-540cbca63c43",
                        "entry_id": "a3e7fa39-b0f5-3492-b1c1-327539e6ba29",
                        "glosses": [
                            "drobny przedmiot lub znak przypominający jakieś zdarzenie, miejsce albo osobę"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "17271247-88ae-4097-a3d3-293d4f88b38a",
                                "sense_id": "319085eb-cc17-31d6-83d0-540cbca63c43",
                                "text": "Z każdych zagranicznych wakacji przywozimy mnóstwo pamiątek."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "09c9b1a0-0f0e-4de7-b21b-6cff6f8245fc",
                                "sense_id": "319085eb-cc17-31d6-83d0-540cbca63c43",
                                "text": "Spójrz, ta blizna to pamiątka po operacji."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "73cd4c0a-1600-42a4-addf-4697d8e46494",
                        "source_entry_id": "a3e7fa39-b0f5-3492-b1c1-327539e6ba29",
                        "source_sense_id": "319085eb-cc17-31d6-83d0-540cbca63c43",
                        "target_lang_word": "keepsake",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "keepsake",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "05ca7bb2-26fb-3285-bc17-5aba3ea9abf2",
                                        "entry_id": "42fd0cbd-84c0-37a6-9d3e-68c009165989",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An object given by a person and retained in memory of something or someone; something kept for sentimental or nostalgic reasons."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "caabfea4-3e1d-41cf-bb52-8e63981079c2",
                                                "sense_id": "05ca7bb2-26fb-3285-bc17-5aba3ea9abf2",
                                                "text": "And yet I should have dearly liked, I own, to have touched her lips; to have questioned her, that she might have opened them; to have looked upon the lashes of her downcast eyes, and never raised a blush; to have let loose waves of hair, an inch of which would be a keepsake beyond price: in short, I should have liked, I do confess, to have had the lightest licence of a child, and yet to have been man enough to know its value."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64142236-bfa2-418f-b2de-7eae365ce19d",
                                                "sense_id": "05ca7bb2-26fb-3285-bc17-5aba3ea9abf2",
                                                "text": "My little keepsake—only a brooch—lay on the table at her bedside, with her prayer-book, and the miniature portrait of her father which she takes with her wherever she goes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64d9597f-0b5c-4cfb-856f-dc6f575c5e3e",
                                                "sense_id": "05ca7bb2-26fb-3285-bc17-5aba3ea9abf2",
                                                "text": "He wished you to have it, as a little keepsake he had prepared—it is only a purse, Miss Wilfer—but as he was disappointed in his fancy, I volunteered to come after you with it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c99991bd-87d6-47a4-b606-7df9e82fa51a",
                                                "sense_id": "05ca7bb2-26fb-3285-bc17-5aba3ea9abf2",
                                                "text": "It seemed to me that if I owned an elephant that was a keepsake, and I thought a good deal of him, I would think twice before I would ride him over that bridge."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f3a253b-89d5-4963-ac7b-5bca78851743",
                                                "sense_id": "05ca7bb2-26fb-3285-bc17-5aba3ea9abf2",
                                                "text": "He walked on hastily, and as he went he hid Jezebel's keepsake first under his cloak, and then deeper, under the sober grey justicor, or waistcoat, near the place where his Presbyterian heart was beating all too unsoberly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "029cbd2e-82b4-4692-b71d-acaa589e8559",
                                                "sense_id": "05ca7bb2-26fb-3285-bc17-5aba3ea9abf2",
                                                "text": "Clam-shells are fashionable keepsakes. You write your name and the date inside one and your friend writes hers in the other and you exchange."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb5d64b3-0ce9-47a3-a2d3-c7d58848577f",
                                                "sense_id": "05ca7bb2-26fb-3285-bc17-5aba3ea9abf2",
                                                "text": "Meghan’s growing list of As Ever products includes a crepe mix, a shortbread mix with flower sprinkles, apricot spread in “keepsake packaging”, a limited-edition orange blossom honey and various teas."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2bb4cc9b-1550-3819-abb1-3a0fc4252de2",
                                        "entry_id": "42fd0cbd-84c0-37a6-9d3e-68c009165989",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Specifically, a type of literary album popular in the nineteenth-century, containing scraps of poetry and prose, and engravings."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0419fc5a-2e17-41f7-94e9-2ac7d3b02fdd",
                                                "sense_id": "2bb4cc9b-1550-3819-abb1-3a0fc4252de2",
                                                "text": "He had brought the last “Keepsake,” the gorgeous watered-silk publication which marked modern progress at that time; and he considered himself very fortunate that he could be the first to look over it with her, dwelling on the ladies and gentlemen with shiny copper-plate cheeks and copper-plate smiles, and pointing to comic verses as capital and sentimental stories as interesting."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38206b91-db1b-42ff-8336-7d74ebf15ea2",
                                                "sense_id": "2bb4cc9b-1550-3819-abb1-3a0fc4252de2",
                                                "text": "[…]it was the Italy that we know from the steel engravings in old keepsakes and annuals, from the vignettes on music-sheets and the drop-curtains at theatres; an Italy that we can never confess to ourselves—in spite of our own changes and of Italy’s—that we have ceased to believe in."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "84082f06-b991-495b-b67e-8fa718b0198d",
                        "source_entry_id": "a3e7fa39-b0f5-3492-b1c1-327539e6ba29",
                        "source_sense_id": "319085eb-cc17-31d6-83d0-540cbca63c43",
                        "target_lang_word": "souvenir",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "souvenir",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0d5fa41d-455b-31fa-9728-ab25a23eaef7",
                                        "entry_id": "c50a5dbd-a6da-3d3a-9f6e-0f82f555af9f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An item of sentimental value, that is given or kept to remember an event or location."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4030749e-7830-4a1e-84a6-b07cf4e0677a",
                                                "sense_id": "0d5fa41d-455b-31fa-9728-ab25a23eaef7",
                                                "text": "Back then, nobody knew in the schoolyard\nNow then, you have grown up to be this hard\nGo then, walk through this world with your heart scarred\nYou're the souvenir of sadness"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d38152a5-271e-4db3-8574-f930913e386a",
                                                "sense_id": "0d5fa41d-455b-31fa-9728-ab25a23eaef7",
                                                "text": "The tourists stuck to the safe confines of the gift shop, where they bought souvenir combs, shot glasses, oversize pencils, and blocks of cedar painted with rhyming poems and shellacked to a high gloss."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "souvenir",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3850255a-9903-3c6b-95ae-babc7651bed5",
                                        "entry_id": "062c9f42-4333-3c3a-8917-3ffd956c2cd0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To take (something) as a souvenir, especially illicitly, for example during wartime."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a52744a0-fb0e-478e-b178-8d7975b6cf18",
                                                "sense_id": "3850255a-9903-3c6b-95ae-babc7651bed5",
                                                "text": "\"Doubletime up to the ville and souvenir me one cute orphan, man, but be sure you get a dirty one, a really skuzzy one.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "879ec57d-821f-4780-acb9-5b3d8caa0029",
                                                "sense_id": "3850255a-9903-3c6b-95ae-babc7651bed5",
                                                "text": "The word is they're waiting for some blokes who had gone off souveniring before the order was announced."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b4f0043f-f8ea-4b3b-a775-837bc0888695",
                        "source_entry_id": "a3e7fa39-b0f5-3492-b1c1-327539e6ba29",
                        "source_sense_id": "319085eb-cc17-31d6-83d0-540cbca63c43",
                        "target_lang_word": "memento",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "memento",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "137124e7-966f-3318-84ec-13c5c58423a6",
                                        "entry_id": "6ac0cfc3-e4cd-3d99-a234-018f30a4a30b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A keepsake; an object kept as a reminder of a place or event."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b741b763-c3ee-4189-80f5-6b0de03ac79f",
                                                "sense_id": "137124e7-966f-3318-84ec-13c5c58423a6",
                                                "text": "I kept the shell as a memento of my visit to the seashore."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e6ed166-68fa-4ab8-be3e-e6ca55db7b07",
                                                "sense_id": "137124e7-966f-3318-84ec-13c5c58423a6",
                                                "text": "In conclusion, I would remark that the great railway stations of London deserve to be visited every whit as much as St. Paul's Cathedral, the Abbey, or the Tower, and they are as worthy a memento of this century as those buildings are of the days that are gone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49e30c4c-6388-4ece-b6b1-545d003fda99",
                                                "sense_id": "137124e7-966f-3318-84ec-13c5c58423a6",
                                                "text": "Many hospitals have not taken simple steps to lessen the distress and confusion which dementia sufferers' often feel on being somewhere so unfamiliar – such as making signs large and easy to read, using colour schemes to help patients find their way around unfamiliar wards and not putting family mementoes such as photographs nearby."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a3a286ac-dc7e-4728-8b9d-fea4280c1275",
                        "source_entry_id": "a3e7fa39-b0f5-3492-b1c1-327539e6ba29",
                        "source_sense_id": "319085eb-cc17-31d6-83d0-540cbca63c43",
